      "writtenOn": "2026-04-13T13:02:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like you are right...\n\nIn the `virtio-drivers` crate (used by both pvmfw and Trusty) the PKVM_GHC_IOWRITE hypercall used to use `in` (not `inout`) for rax. That was indirectly fixed by https://github.com/rcore-os/virtio-drivers/commit/2e7b9ce3cc0d9f2346d89ad703cb17c86f756ca5.\n\nBut it turns out that for some reason we have two different forks of this crate: `virtio-drivers` used by pvmfw and `virtio-drivers-and-devices` used by Trusty.\n\n`virtio-drivers-and-devices` includes the fix, so it uses `inout` for rax for any hypercalls: https://googleplex-android.googlesource.com/platform/external/rust/android-crates-io/+/refs/heads/main/crates/virtio-drivers-and-devices/src/transport/x86_64/hypercalls.rs#59\n\nbut `virtio-drivers` still doesn\u0027t include it, so it still uses `in` for rax in PKVM_GHC_IOWRITE: https://googleplex-android.googlesource.com/platform/external/rust/android-crates-io/+/refs/heads/main/crates/virtio-drivers/src/transport/x86_64/hypercalls.rs#81\n\n@jaszczyk@google.com can we update the `virtio-drivers` fork?",
      "parentUuid": "584d016d_d8836f29",
      "revId": "ec68b9638cdd7c06a224c81eb4b6a188cf93409e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
